#{[{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186096621 :knowledge-point/canonical-example {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186096421 :question/id #uuid "f804809a-22bf-5ab3-9775-3591d4581797" :question/math-academy-id "e-3638" :question/problem "If $f(x)=\\dfrac{1+\\sin x}{x},$ find $f'(x).$" :question/worked-solution "In this case, the expression for $f(x)$ is a quotient $\\dfrac{u(x)}{v(x)}$ with $u(x) = 1+\\sin x$ and $v(x) = x.$ \n\nTherefore, we apply the quotient rule as follows:\n\n$$\n\\eqalign{\nf'(x) & = \\dfrac{u'(x)\\cdot v(x) - u(x)\\cdot v'(x)}{[v(x)]^2}\\\n\t\t         \t& = \\dfrac{(1+\\sin x)'\\cdot (x) -(1+\\sin x)\\cdot (x)'}{x^2}\\\n\t\t\t        & = \\dfrac{\\cos x \\cdot x- (1+\\sin x)\\cdot 1}{x^2}\\\n\t\t\t\t& = \\dfrac{x \\cos x -\\sin x -1}{x^2}\t\t\t\n}\n$$"} :knowledge-point/id #uuid "3c547746-49c8-5a4a-85fe-c6b75493a354" :knowledge-point/key-prerequisites [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186048749 :topic/math-academy-id 1114 :topic/title "Differentiating Exponential Functions"} {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186050420 :topic/math-academy-id 280 :topic/title "Differentiating Trigonometric Functions"} {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186050690 :topic/math-academy-id 1116 :topic/title "Differentiating Logarithmic Functions"}] :knowledge-point/questions [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186097141 :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "ce366287-456c-5eb0-a5d5-2adc608bebdf" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\frac{x\\cos x\\ln x - \\cos x}{x\\ln^{2} x}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186094820} {:answer/id #uuid "db4448aa-0913-5a6d-a5bd-9a63960529a3" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\frac{x\\sin x\\ln x - \\cos x}{x\\sin^{2} x}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186094821} {:answer/id #uuid "f3ffa073-4b42-510d-a5f6-21b24adf2312" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\frac{\\sin x\\ln x - \\cos x}{x\\ln^{2} x}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186094822} {:answer/id #uuid "4d78886d-eb37-51f0-999a-21157f737565" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\frac{-x\\sin x\\ln x - \\cos x}{x\\ln^{2} x}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186094823} {:answer/id #uuid "57cbf897-170a-57f8-aa5a-9204f74cbb1d" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\frac{-\\sin x\\ln x - \\sin x}{x\\ln^{2} x}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186094824}] :answer-field/id #uuid "9a8ab129-c812-5393-b846-093adcba9f35" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type {:db/ident :answer-field.type/radio} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186094819}] :question/id #uuid "eaaa6afe-d8c3-5b2c-aab7-da09c5bd5e57" :question/math-academy-id "q-17921" :question/problem "If $f(x) = \\frac{\\cos x}{\\ln x}$, find $f^{′}(x)$."} {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186097246 :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "a696f24c-5a22-51df-8fea-714b0d378534" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\frac{2\\sin x - x\\cos x}{\\sin^{2} x}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186095401} {:answer/id #uuid "b9fa229a-1868-577c-8d7e-68ec1a926b00" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "(x(\\sin x - 2\\cos x))/(\\sin x)" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186095402} {:answer/id #uuid "d64e7a52-b89a-59b6-8cec-f246848d6644" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "(x(2\\cos x - x\\sin x))/(\\sin^{2} x)" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186095403} {:answer/id #uuid "fa8f70f4-0795-5d97-9b22-acaf08d99845" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "(x(2\\sin x - x\\cos x))/(\\sin^{2} x)" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186095404} {:answer/id #uuid "69543e94-b7f1-525e-928e-241edb2840c2" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "(x(2\\sin x + x\\cos x))/(\\sin^{2} x)" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186095405}] :answer-field/id #uuid "4f2d5ea5-0cb5-568d-92ce-6b7104f4ce12" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type {:db/ident :answer-field.type/radio} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186095400}] :question/id #uuid "b2f7cbd7-3024-5a15-be08-bc174e3f7f50" :question/math-academy-id "q-47999" :question/problem "If $f(x) = \\frac{x^{2}}{\\sin x}$, find $f^{′}(x)$."} {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186233908 :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "86c3e4cd-220c-5b44-9e47-247e8aa818dc" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "-\\frac{2}{{e}^{3}}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186232826}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "86c3e4cd-220c-5b44-9e47-247e8aa818dc" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "-\\frac{2}{{e}^{3}}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186232826} :answer-field/id #uuid "1b4ca45e-0b0b-566c-9bac-475ecb225906" :answer-field/key "field-1" :answer-field/type {:db/ident :answer-field.type/blank} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186232825}] :question/difficulty {:db/ident :question.difficulty/moderate} :question/id #uuid "223b6a86-4eab-562a-a794-2f6a06bf3dd3" :question/math-academy-id "q-340318" :question/problem "If a curve $C$ is given by $y=\\frac{x}{{e}^{3x}},$ calculate the slope of the tangent line to the curve at the point where $x=1.$\n\nThe slope at $x=1$ is\n{{field-1}}." :question/worked-solution "In this case, the expression for $y$ is a quotient $\\frac{u(x)}{v(x)}$ with $u(x)=x$ and $v(x)={e}^{3x}.$ \n\nTherefore, we apply the quotient rule as follows:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{f}^{'}(x) & =\\frac{{u}^{'}(x)\\cdot v(x)-u(x)\\cdot {v}^{'}(x)}{[v(x)]^{2}} \\\\  & =\\frac{{(x)}^{'}\\cdot {e}^{3x}-x\\cdot {({e}^{3x})}^{'}}{{({e}^{3x})}^{2}} \\\\  & =\\frac{1\\cdot {e}^{3x}-x\\cdot 3{e}^{3x}}{{({e}^{3x})}^{2}} \\\\  & =\\frac{{e}^{3x}(1-3x)}{{({e}^{3x})}^{2}} \\\\  & =\\frac{1-3x}{{e}^{3x}}\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nTo find the slope of the tangent line, we now substitute $x=1$ into the formula and get\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{f}^{'}\\,(1) & =\\frac{1-3(1)}{{e}^{3(1)}} \\\\  & =\\frac{-2}{{e}^{3}} \\\\  & =-\\frac{2}{{e}^{3}}.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nTherefore, the slope of the tangent line at $x=1$ is $-\\frac{2}{{e}^{3}}.$"} {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186234507 :question/difficulty {:db/ident :question.difficulty/moderate} :question/id #uuid "2e9ec61c-a65c-56b3-820e-2d60ba70912c" :question/math-academy-id "q-9908" :question/problem "If a curve $C$ is given by $y=\\frac{\\operatorname{cos}x}{1+\\operatorname{sin}x},$ calculate the slope of the tangent line to the curve at the point where $x=\\frac{\\pi }{2}.$" :question/worked-solution "In this case, the expression for $y$ is a quotient $\\frac{u(x)}{v(x)}$ with $u(x)=\\operatorname{cos}x$ and $v(x)=1+\\operatorname{sin}x.$ \n\nTherefore, we apply the quotient rule as follows:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{f}^{'}(x) & =\\frac{{u}^{'}(x)\\cdot v(x)-u(x)\\cdot {v}^{'}(x)}{[v(x)]^{2}} \\\\  & =\\frac{(\\operatorname{cos}x)^{'}\\cdot (1+\\operatorname{sin}x)-\\operatorname{cos}x\\cdot (1+\\operatorname{sin}x)^{'}}{(1+\\operatorname{sin}x)^{2}} \\\\  & =\\frac{(-\\operatorname{sin}x)(1+\\operatorname{sin}x)-(\\operatorname{cos}x)\\operatorname{cos}x}{(1+\\operatorname{sin}x)^{2}} \\\\  & =\\frac{(-\\operatorname{sin}x-{sin}^{2}x-{cos}^{2}x)}{(1+\\operatorname{sin}x)^{2}} \\\\  & =\\frac{(-\\operatorname{sin}x-({sin}^{2}x+{cos}^{2}x))}{(1+\\operatorname{sin}x)^{2}}\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\n Since ${sin}^{2}x+{cos}^{2}x=1$, we have\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{f}^{'}(x) & =\\frac{(-\\operatorname{sin}x-1)}{(1+\\operatorname{sin}x)^{2}} \\\\  & =\\frac{-(1+\\operatorname{sin}x)}{(1+\\operatorname{sin}x)^{2}} \\\\  & =-\\frac{1}{1+\\operatorname{sin}x}.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nTo find the slope of the tangent line, we now substitute $x=\\frac{\\pi }{2}$ into the formula and get\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{f}^{'}(\\frac{\\pi }{2}) & =-\\frac{1}{1+\\operatorname{sin}(\\frac{\\pi }{2})} \\\\  & =-\\frac{1}{1+1} \\\\  & =-\\frac{1}{2}.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nTherefore, the slope of the tangent line is $-\\frac{1}{2}.$"} {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186235433 :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "16242856-ba0f-5959-96a9-cc84fceb8d9c" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\frac{{e}^{x}(\\operatorname{cos}x-\\operatorname{sin}x)}{8{sin}^{2}x}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186234573}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "16242856-ba0f-5959-96a9-cc84fceb8d9c" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\frac{{e}^{x}(\\operatorname{cos}x-\\operatorname{sin}x)}{8{sin}^{2}x}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186234573} :answer-field/id #uuid "7da92529-d318-5dfa-bfa7-0df43fae7490" :answer-field/key "field-1" :answer-field/type {:db/ident :answer-field.type/blank} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186235128}] :question/difficulty {:db/ident :question.difficulty/easy} :question/id #uuid "8c7fd239-c698-5700-aea8-d260b2cef38a" :question/math-academy-id "q-167328" :question/problem "$\\frac{\\text{d}}{\\text{d}x}(\\frac{f}{h})\\,=$\n\n                            \n                                    \n                            \n                                        {{field-1}}" :question/worked-solution "Recall that $f(x)=\\frac{1}{2}{e}^{x}$ and $h(x)=-4\\operatorname{sin}⁡x.$\n\nWe apply the quotient rule, as follows:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\frac{\\text{d}}{\\text{d}x}(\\frac{f}{h}) & =\\frac{{f}^{′}(x)\\cdot h(x)-f(x)\\cdot {h}^{′}(x)}{[h(x)]^{2}} \\\\  & =\\frac{{(\\frac{1}{2}{e}^{x})}^{′}\\cdot (-4\\operatorname{sin}⁡x)-(\\frac{1}{2}{e}^{x})\\cdot (-4\\operatorname{sin}⁡x)^{′}}{(-4\\operatorname{sin}⁡x)^{2}} \\\\  & =\\frac{(\\frac{1}{2}{e}^{x})\\cdot (-4\\operatorname{sin}⁡x)-(\\frac{1}{2}{e}^{x})\\cdot (-4\\operatorname{cos}⁡x)}{16{sin}^{2}⁡x} \\\\  & =\\frac{2{e}^{x}(\\operatorname{cos}⁡x-\\operatorname{sin}⁡x)}{16{sin}^{2}⁡x} \\\\  & =\\frac{{e}^{x}(\\operatorname{cos}⁡x-\\operatorname{sin}⁡x)}{8{sin}^{2}⁡x}\\end{aligned}\n$$"} {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186235481 :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "32ae6381-27b6-5f93-8131-98453b145862" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\operatorname{cos}(x)-\\operatorname{sin}(x)" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186234625}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "32ae6381-27b6-5f93-8131-98453b145862" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\operatorname{cos}(x)-\\operatorname{sin}(x)" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186234625} :answer-field/id #uuid "90dbff55-8f3a-5c54-81ca-c8b7d5227587" :answer-field/key "field-1" :answer-field/type {:db/ident :answer-field.type/blank} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186235146}] :question/difficulty {:db/ident :question.difficulty/easy} :question/id #uuid "a4ea7df7-6856-52ff-9d9c-29beb9f68c2e" :question/math-academy-id "q-167782" :question/problem "Calculate $\\frac{\\text{d}}{\\text{d}x}(\\frac{f}{h}).$\n\n                            \n                                    \n                                        \n                                        \n\n| $\\frac{\\text{d}}{\\text{d}x}(\\frac{f}{h})\\,=\\,\\,$ | ${e}^{x}($\n\n                                    \n                                \n                                    \n                            \n                                        {{field-1}}                \n                                    \n                                \n                                    \n                                        \n                                         $)$ |\n| --- | --- |\n| $8{sin}^{2}⁡(x)$ |  |" :question/worked-solution "Recall that $f(x)=\\frac{1}{2}{e}^{x}$ and $h(x)=-4\\operatorname{sin}⁡(x).$\n\nWe apply the quotient rule, as follows:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\frac{\\text{d}}{\\text{d}x}(\\frac{f}{h}) & =\\frac{{f}^{′}(x)\\cdot h(x)-f(x)\\cdot {h}^{′}(x)}{[h(x)]^{2}} \\\\  & =\\frac{{(\\frac{1}{2}{e}^{x})}^{′}\\cdot (-4\\operatorname{sin}⁡(x))-(\\frac{1}{2}{e}^{x})\\cdot (-4\\operatorname{sin}⁡(x))^{′}}{(-4\\operatorname{sin}⁡(x))^{2}} \\\\  & =\\frac{(\\frac{1}{2}{e}^{x})\\cdot (-4\\operatorname{sin}⁡(x))-(\\frac{1}{2}{e}^{x})\\cdot (-4\\operatorname{cos}⁡(x))}{16{sin}^{2}⁡(x)} \\\\  & =\\frac{2{e}^{x}(\\operatorname{cos}⁡(x)-\\operatorname{sin}⁡(x))}{16{sin}^{2}⁡(x)} \\\\  & =\\frac{{e}^{x}(\\operatorname{cos}⁡(x)-\\operatorname{sin}⁡(x))}{8{sin}^{2}⁡(x)}\\end{aligned}\n$$"} {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186290512 :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "08139daf-29b8-522c-86f5-f4b319f2f128" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\frac{{x}^{2}sin⁡x-2cos⁡x}{10{x}^{3}}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186288095} {:answer/id #uuid "1e48d6b6-0438-5f89-a52d-d8eb2780f6d0" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\frac{xsin⁡x-2cos⁡x}{10{x}^{4}}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186288226} {:answer/id #uuid "325a8965-b65d-5099-9f7f-4f1627e15fe6" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\frac{sin⁡x-cos⁡x}{10{x}^{3}}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186288360} {:answer/id #uuid "35245c0f-50c6-5ecf-911b-c14b9458549b" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\frac{-xsin⁡x-2cos⁡x}{10{x}^{3}}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186288387} {:answer/id #uuid "f8a5b569-bd3b-52ae-9b0c-22db66e06b6e" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\frac{sin⁡x-2cos⁡x}{10{x}^{3}}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186289668}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "35245c0f-50c6-5ecf-911b-c14b9458549b" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\frac{-xsin⁡x-2cos⁡x}{10{x}^{3}}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186288387} :answer-field/id #uuid "b894772b-c0c7-50ad-9f3f-8c10e4604ab7" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type {:db/ident :answer-field.type/radio} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186290134}] :question/difficulty {:db/ident :question.difficulty/easy} :question/id #uuid "3b0fa11c-feb9-540f-a74b-38792fbe2335" :question/math-academy-id "q-2385" :question/problem "If $f(x)=\\frac{cos⁡x}{10{x}^{2}},$ find ${f}^{′}(x).$" :question/worked-solution "In this case, the expression for $f(x)$ is a quotient $\\frac{u(x)}{v(x)}$ with $u(x)=cos⁡x$ and $v(x)=10{x}^{2}.$ \n\nTherefore, we apply the quotient rule as follows:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\begin{aligned}{f}^{′}(x) & =\\frac{{u}^{′}(x)\\cdot v(x)-u(x)\\cdot {v}^{′}(x)}{[v(x)]^{2}} \\\\  & =\\frac{(-sin⁡x)(10{x}^{2})-(cos⁡x)(20x)}{(10{x}^{2})^{2}} \\\\  & =\\frac{-10{x}^{2}sin⁡x-20xcos⁡x}{100{x}^{4}} \\\\  & =\\frac{\\cancel{10x}(-xsin⁡x-2cos⁡x)}{\\cancel{10x}\\cdot 10{x}^{3}} \\\\  & =\\frac{-xsin⁡x-2cos⁡x}{10{x}^{3}}\\end{aligned}\\end{aligned}\n$$"} {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186314927 :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "bbaaae38-fd03-521a-987f-003fe81bd8ba" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\frac{x{sec}^{2}x-\\operatorname{tan}x}{{x}^{2}}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186313438}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "bbaaae38-fd03-521a-987f-003fe81bd8ba" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\frac{x{sec}^{2}x-\\operatorname{tan}x}{{x}^{2}}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186313438} :answer-field/id #uuid "444462bc-40fb-5b71-86e8-ac7080c78e9b" :answer-field/key "field-1" :answer-field/type {:db/ident :answer-field.type/blank} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186314197}] :question/difficulty {:db/ident :question.difficulty/easy} :question/id #uuid "18258014-36f7-5eab-9f3f-292a9627b048" :question/math-academy-id "q-340308" :question/problem "If $f(x)=\\frac{tan⁡x}{x}$,  find ${f}^{′}(x).$\n\n${f}^{′}(x)=$\n{{field-1}}" :question/worked-solution "In this case, the expression for $f(x)$ is a quotient $\\frac{u(x)}{v(x)}$ with $u(x)=tan⁡x$ and $v(x)=x.$ \n\nTherefore, we apply the quotient rule as follows:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{f}^{′}(x) & =\\frac{{u}^{′}(x)\\cdot v(x)-u(x)\\cdot {v}^{′}(x)}{[v(x)]^{2}} \\\\  & =\\frac{(tan⁡x)^{′}\\cdot x-tan⁡x\\cdot (x)^{′}}{{x}^{2}} \\\\  & =\\frac{{sec}^{2}⁡x\\cdot x-tan⁡x\\cdot 1}{{x}^{2}} \\\\  & =\\frac{x{sec}^{2}⁡x-tan⁡x}{{x}^{2}}\\end{aligned}\n$$"} {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186314928 :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "43024ff2-7333-5aaf-9591-019e27a3d6e8" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\frac{\\operatorname{sin}x-x\\operatorname{cos}x}{{sin}^{2}x}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186312509}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "43024ff2-7333-5aaf-9591-019e27a3d6e8" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\frac{\\operatorname{sin}x-x\\operatorname{cos}x}{{sin}^{2}x}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186312509} :answer-field/id #uuid "6587bb6d-addc-5565-8d8b-182baf9e3e12" :answer-field/key "field-1" :answer-field/type {:db/ident :answer-field.type/blank} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186314294}] :question/difficulty {:db/ident :question.difficulty/easy} :question/id #uuid "10dcc430-0a77-5b8b-9487-843346dfaa0d" :question/math-academy-id "q-340309" :question/problem "If $f(x)=\\frac{x}{sin⁡x},$ find ${f}^{′}(x).$\n\n${f}^{′}(x)=$\n{{field-1}}" :question/worked-solution "In this case, the expression for $f(x)$ is a quotient $\\frac{u(x)}{v(x)}$ with $u(x)=x$ and $v(x)=sin⁡x.$ \n\nTherefore, we apply the quotient rule as follows:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{f}^{′}(x) & =\\frac{{u}^{′}(x)\\cdot v(x)-u(x)\\cdot {v}^{′}(x)}{[v(x)]^{2}} \\\\  & =\\frac{(x)^{′}\\cdot sin⁡x-x\\cdot (sin⁡x)^{′}}{{(sin⁡x)}^{2}} \\\\  & =\\frac{1\\cdot sin⁡x-x\\cdot cos⁡x}{{sin}^{2}⁡x} \\\\  & =\\frac{sin⁡x-xcos⁡x}{{sin}^{2}⁡x}\\end{aligned}\n$$"} {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186314929 :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "030817a4-5c86-5a0e-952e-cf5f2fb1ae18" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "-\\operatorname{ln}2" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186311984}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "030817a4-5c86-5a0e-952e-cf5f2fb1ae18" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "-\\operatorname{ln}2" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186311984} :answer-field/id #uuid "99739388-4d18-5c69-8fdc-dc054d584966" :answer-field/key "field-1" :answer-field/type {:db/ident :answer-field.type/blank} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186314427}] :question/difficulty {:db/ident :question.difficulty/moderate} :question/id #uuid "1df174b4-8cf7-500c-9fc1-5a7ed4adda8f" :question/math-academy-id "q-340316" :question/problem "If a curve $C$ is given by $y=\\frac{{2}^{x}}{{x}^{2}-1},$ calculate the slope of the tangent line to the curve at the point where $x=0.$\n\nThe slope at $x=0$ is\n{{field-1}}." :question/worked-solution "In this case, the expression for $y$ is a quotient $\\frac{u(x)}{v(x)}$ with $u(x)={2}^{x}$ and $v(x)={x}^{2}-1.$ \n\nTherefore, we apply the quotient rule as follows:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{f}^{′}(x) & =\\frac{{u}^{′}(x)\\cdot v(x)-u(x)\\cdot {v}^{′}(x)}{[v(x)]^{2}} \\\\  & =\\frac{{({2}^{x})}^{′}\\cdot ({x}^{2}-1)-{2}^{x}\\cdot {({x}^{2}-1)}^{′}}{{({x}^{2}-1)}^{2}} \\\\  & =\\frac{{2}^{x}ln⁡2\\cdot ({x}^{2}-1)-{2}^{x}\\cdot 2x}{{({x}^{2}-1)}^{2}} \\\\  & =\\frac{{2}^{x}[({x}^{2}-1)ln⁡2-2x]}{{({x}^{2}-1)}^{2}}\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nTo find the slope of the tangent line, we now substitute $x=0$ into the formula and get\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{f}^{′}\\,(0) & =\\frac{{2}^{0}[({0}^{2}-1)ln⁡2-2(0)]}{{({0}^{2}-1)}^{2}} \\\\  & =\\frac{-ln⁡2}{1} \\\\  & =-ln⁡2.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nTherefore, the slope of the tangent line at $x=0$ is $-ln⁡2.$"} {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186329841 :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "24cdb15d-92a4-57bb-b3ae-70ee6398efed" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\frac{{e}^{x}sin⁡x-cos⁡x}{{sin}^{2}⁡x}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186327252} {:answer/id #uuid "28cffc72-f500-56eb-b62d-297789e3d352" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\frac{{e}^{x}(cos⁡x+sin⁡x)}{{cos}^{2}⁡x}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186327280} {:answer/id #uuid "537f4f22-dc76-5ecc-941c-28735a7fbb3e" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\frac{{e}^{x}sin⁡x-cos⁡x}{{cos}^{2}⁡x}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186327658} {:answer/id #uuid "6cb04a5b-8198-547f-9f85-6d03684ff103" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\frac{{e}^{x}(sin⁡x-cos⁡x)}{cos⁡x}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186327873} {:answer/id #uuid "6ebf154b-78ed-5323-9bc6-5af4e4ce0e17" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\frac{{e}^{x}(sin⁡x-cos⁡x)}{{cos}^{2}⁡x}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186327893}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "28cffc72-f500-56eb-b62d-297789e3d352" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\frac{{e}^{x}(cos⁡x+sin⁡x)}{{cos}^{2}⁡x}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186327280} :answer-field/id #uuid "1139e71c-df1c-5f00-8bad-e71886ea7ae5" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type {:db/ident :answer-field.type/radio} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186329215}] :question/difficulty {:db/ident :question.difficulty/easy} :question/id #uuid "5ace0fb1-1a71-5cfd-952c-d11857b972c9" :question/math-academy-id "q-47943" :question/problem "If $f(x)=\\frac{{e}^{x}}{cos⁡x},$ find ${f}^{′}(x).$" :question/worked-solution "In this case, the expression for $f(x)$ is a quotient $\\frac{u(x)}{v(x)}$ with $u(x)={e}^{x}$ and $v(x)=cos⁡x.$ \n\nTherefore, we apply the quotient rule as follows:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\begin{aligned}{f}^{′}(x) & =\\frac{{u}^{′}(x)\\cdot v(x)-u(x)\\cdot {v}^{′}(x)}{[v(x)]^{2}} \\\\  & =\\frac{({e}^{x})^{′}\\cdot cos⁡x-{e}^{x}\\cdot (cos⁡x)^{′}}{(cos⁡x)^{2}} \\\\  & =\\frac{{e}^{x}cos⁡x+{e}^{x}sin⁡x}{(cos⁡x)^{2}} \\\\  & =\\frac{{e}^{x}(cos⁡x+sin⁡x)}{{cos}^{2}⁡x}\\end{aligned}\\end{aligned}\n$$"} {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186329849 :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "5d04b0f4-3b5e-5a83-ab7c-fadd2fae0aa3" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\frac{xcos⁡x+2sin⁡x}{{x}^{3}}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186327753} {:answer/id #uuid "79438a62-c77a-5744-9802-65b0e97ef42c" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\frac{cos⁡x-2xsin⁡x}{{x}^{4}}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186327973} {:answer/id #uuid "85f38040-e7a5-59fd-a359-c862f85f6a27" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\frac{xcos⁡x-2sin⁡x}{{x}^{3}}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186328088} {:answer/id #uuid "a8c4ce4c-f609-552a-9123-d8fd254ccab0" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\frac{2xcos⁡x-xsin⁡x}{{x}^{3}}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186328396} {:answer/id #uuid "c0e8be1f-f487-5a62-b564-e74b12097ed9" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\frac{xsin⁡x-2cos⁡x}{{x}^{4}}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186328619}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "85f38040-e7a5-59fd-a359-c862f85f6a27" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\frac{xcos⁡x-2sin⁡x}{{x}^{3}}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186328088} :answer-field/id #uuid "9f86cadc-4440-532f-bf1a-6161f5f6bfb9" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type {:db/ident :answer-field.type/radio} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186329450}] :question/difficulty {:db/ident :question.difficulty/easy} :question/id #uuid "b3c4b5b5-b682-57e6-baf5-0601260b1ed0" :question/math-academy-id "q-47998" :question/problem "If $f(x)=\\frac{sin⁡x}{{x}^{2}},$ find ${f}^{′}(x).$" :question/worked-solution "In this case, the expression for $f(x)$ is a quotient $\\frac{u(x)}{v(x)}$ with $u(x)=sin⁡x$ and $v(x)={x}^{2}.$ \n\nTherefore, we apply the quotient rule as follows:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\begin{aligned}{f}^{′}(x) & =\\frac{{u}^{′}(x)\\cdot v(x)-u(x)\\cdot {v}^{′}(x)}{[v(x)]^{2}} \\\\  & =\\frac{(sin⁡x)^{′}\\cdot {x}^{2}-sin⁡x\\cdot ({x}^{2})^{′}}{({x}^{2})^{2}} \\\\  & =\\frac{{x}^{2}cos⁡x-2xsin⁡x}{{x}^{4}} \\\\  & =\\frac{x(xcos⁡x-2sin⁡x)}{{x}^{4}} \\\\  & =\\frac{xcos⁡x-2sin⁡x}{{x}^{3}}\\end{aligned}\\end{aligned}\n$$"} {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186329887 :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "22e53f34-1f08-55ea-b027-91a6570c9ba2" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "e" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186327234} {:answer/id #uuid "9d3be258-9fcf-5d57-a47f-1395e89bbde9" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\frac{1}{4}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186328293} {:answer/id #uuid "c4c08959-081a-5f50-a3f0-ce4b51612304" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\frac{2}{3}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186328658} {:answer/id #uuid "e95dd2da-108e-5550-b9b6-a61109df65bc" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "1" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186328979} {:answer/id #uuid "efde6b46-482d-55c0-a8b0-e2ad91b34126" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\frac{e}{2}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186329029}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "22e53f34-1f08-55ea-b027-91a6570c9ba2" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "e" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186327234} :answer-field/id #uuid "23c86c24-0972-56ca-8779-29609bc15897" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type {:db/ident :answer-field.type/radio} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186329248}] :question/difficulty {:db/ident :question.difficulty/moderate} :question/id #uuid "bf60d52b-f79d-5da2-9400-715a7866a23a" :question/math-academy-id "q-48504" :question/problem "If a curve $C$ is given by $y=\\frac{{x}^{2}}{ln⁡(x)},$ calculate the slope of the tangent line to the curve at the point where $x=e.$" :question/worked-solution "In this case, the expression for $y$ is a quotient $\\frac{u(x)}{v(x)}$ with $u(x)={x}^{2}$ and $v(x)=ln⁡x.$ \n\nTherefore, we apply the quotient rule as follows:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{f}^{′}(x) & =\\frac{{u}^{′}(x)\\cdot v(x)-u(x)\\cdot {v}^{′}(x)}{[v(x)]^{2}} \\\\  & =\\frac{({x}^{2})^{′}\\cdot ln⁡x-{x}^{2}\\cdot (ln⁡x)^{′}}{(ln⁡x)^{2}} \\\\  & =\\frac{2x\\cdot ln⁡(x)-{x}^{2}\\cdot (\\frac{1}{x})}{{(ln⁡(x))}^{2}} \\\\  & =\\frac{2x\\cdot ln⁡(x)-x}{{ln}^{2}⁡(x)} \\\\  & =\\frac{x(2ln⁡(x)-1)}{{ln}^{2}⁡(x)}\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nTo find the slope of the tangent line, we now substitute $x=e$ into the formula and get\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{f}^{′}(e) & =\\frac{e(2ln⁡(e)-1)}{{ln}^{2}⁡(e)} \\\\  & =\\frac{e(2-1)}{{1}^{2}} \\\\  & =e.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nTherefore, the slope of the tangent line is $e.$"} {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186329888 :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "1d637eb0-49d3-5d5a-bc2f-46a3198b126a" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\frac{1}{4\\pi }" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186327188} {:answer/id #uuid "2d2b75a4-6c3e-559a-99f1-a4062d43aa68" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "-\\pi " :db/id #edb/ref 17592186327331} {:answer/id #uuid "9ab0189b-f12c-5d69-a3ac-1572bccacdb1" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "2\\pi " :db/id #edb/ref 17592186328273} {:answer/id #uuid "b66a4a70-89cf-5764-a364-dbddd46ff6e3" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "-\\frac{1}{2}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186328520} {:answer/id #uuid "bd42ca1a-304b-5562-8e62-1ee43deef421" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "-\\frac{1}{2\\pi }" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186328583}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "bd42ca1a-304b-5562-8e62-1ee43deef421" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "-\\frac{1}{2\\pi }" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186328583} :answer-field/id #uuid "a2dfe786-1989-54c2-ac40-7bcf2f579b50" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type {:db/ident :answer-field.type/radio} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186329461}] :question/difficulty {:db/ident :question.difficulty/moderate} :question/id #uuid "e735330d-c2f3-5b05-83d4-12a709d794e0" :question/math-academy-id "q-48507" :question/problem "If a curve $C$ is given by $y=\\frac{sin⁡x}{2x},$ calculate the slope of the tangent line to the curve at the point where $x=\\pi .$" :question/worked-solution "In this case, the expression for $y$ is a quotient $\\frac{u(x)}{v(x)}$ with $u(x)=sin⁡x$ and $v(x)=2x.$ \n\nTherefore, we apply the quotient rule as follows:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{f}^{′}(x) & =\\frac{{u}^{′}(x)\\cdot v(x)-u(x)\\cdot {v}^{′}(x)}{[v(x)]^{2}} \\\\  & =\\frac{(sin⁡x)^{′}\\cdot (2x)-sin⁡x\\cdot (2x)^{′}}{(2x)^{2}} \\\\  & =\\frac{cos⁡x\\cdot (2x)-sin⁡x\\cdot 2}{{(2x)}^{2}} \\\\  & =\\frac{2(xcos⁡x-sin⁡x)}{4{x}^{2}} \\\\  & =\\frac{xcos⁡x-sin⁡x}{2{x}^{2}}\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nTo find the slope of the tangent line, we now substitute $x=\\pi $ into the formula and get\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{f}^{′}(\\pi ) & =\\frac{\\pi cos⁡(\\pi )-sin⁡(\\pi )}{2(\\pi )^{2}} \\\\  & =\\frac{\\pi (-1)-(0)}{2{\\pi }^{2}} \\\\  & =-\\frac{\\pi }{2{\\pi }^{2}} \\\\  & =-\\frac{1}{2\\pi }.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nTherefore, the slope of the tangent line is $-\\frac{1}{2\\pi }.$"} {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186488408 :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "230a2bd9-abcc-5289-96ff-2eb4557a322d" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\frac{\\left(2 x + \\cos{\\left(x \\right)}\\right) \\left(e^{x} + 2 \\cos{\\left(x \\right)}\\right) - \\left(x^{2} + \\sin{\\left(x \\right)}\\right) \\left(e^{x} - 2 \\sin{\\left(x \\right)}\\right)}{\\left(x^{2} + \\sin{\\left(x \\right)}\\right)^{2}}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186488411} {:answer/id #uuid "395b417d-4d49-5140-a3a9-4e9e0020ef2e" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\frac{2 x + \\cos{\\left(x \\right)}}{e^{x} - 2 \\sin{\\left(x \\right)}}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186488421} {:answer/id #uuid "3e744e9c-af5e-5ae1-8ffb-1bb4945216c0" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\frac{\\left(2 x + \\cos{\\left(x \\right)}\\right) \\left(e^{x} + 2 \\cos{\\left(x \\right)}\\right) - \\left(x^{2} + \\sin{\\left(x \\right)}\\right) \\left(e^{x} - 2 \\sin{\\left(x \\right)}\\right)}{e^{x} + 2 \\cos{\\left(x \\right)}}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186488423} {:answer/id #uuid "73b42f2e-1517-59f8-819f-e09ced88cb5b" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\frac{\\left(2 x + \\cos{\\left(x \\right)}\\right) \\left(e^{x} + 2 \\cos{\\left(x \\right)}\\right) - \\left(x^{2} + \\sin{\\left(x \\right)}\\right) \\left(e^{x} - 2 \\sin{\\left(x \\right)}\\right)}{\\left(e^{x} + 2 \\cos{\\left(x \\right)}\\right)^{2}}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186488432} {:answer/id #uuid "da5a9944-54a5-5182-9597-9872369d4c5c" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\frac{\\left(2 x + \\cos{\\left(x \\right)}\\right) \\left(e^{x} + 2 \\cos{\\left(x \\right)}\\right) + \\left(x^{2} + \\sin{\\left(x \\right)}\\right) \\left(e^{x} - 2 \\sin{\\left(x \\right)}\\right)}{\\left(e^{x} + 2 \\cos{\\left(x \\right)}\\right)^{2}}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186488444}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "73b42f2e-1517-59f8-819f-e09ced88cb5b" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\frac{\\left(2 x + \\cos{\\left(x \\right)}\\right) \\left(e^{x} + 2 \\cos{\\left(x \\right)}\\right) - \\left(x^{2} + \\sin{\\left(x \\right)}\\right) \\left(e^{x} - 2 \\sin{\\left(x \\right)}\\right)}{\\left(e^{x} + 2 \\cos{\\left(x \\right)}\\right)^{2}}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186488432} :answer-field/id #uuid "e5295c5f-4906-5dc8-bd7a-bed2d6a30c75" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type {:db/ident :answer-field.type/radio} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186488446}] :question/difficulty {:db/ident :question.difficulty/hard} :question/id #uuid "0d6589dd-899d-5e9f-b37f-cdd937732bad" :question/problem "If $f(x)=\\frac{x^{2} + \\sin{\\left(x \\right)}}{e^{x} + 2 \\cos{\\left(x \\right)}}$, find $f^{\\prime}(x)$ wherever the denominator is nonzero." :question/worked-solution "In this case, the expression for $f(x)$ is a quotient $\\frac{u(x)}{v(x)}$ with $u(x)=x^{2} + \\sin{\\left(x \\right)}$ and $v(x)=e^{x} + 2 \\cos{\\left(x \\right)}.$\n\nTherefore, we apply the quotient rule as follows:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}f^{\\prime}(x)&=\\frac{u^{\\prime}(x)\\cdot v(x)-u(x)\\cdot v^{\\prime}(x)}{[v(x)]^{2}}\\\\ &=\\frac{(x^{2} + \\sin{\\left(x \\right)})^{\\prime}\\cdot (e^{x} + 2 \\cos{\\left(x \\right)})-(x^{2} + \\sin{\\left(x \\right)})\\cdot (e^{x} + 2 \\cos{\\left(x \\right)})^{\\prime}}{(e^{x} + 2 \\cos{\\left(x \\right)})^{2}}\\\\ &=\\frac{(2 x + \\cos{\\left(x \\right)})\\cdot (e^{x} + 2 \\cos{\\left(x \\right)})-(x^{2} + \\sin{\\left(x \\right)})\\cdot (e^{x} - 2 \\sin{\\left(x \\right)})}{(e^{x} + 2 \\cos{\\left(x \\right)})^{2}}\\\\ &=\\frac{2 x^{2} \\sin{\\left(x \\right)} + 4 x \\cos{\\left(x \\right)} + \\left(- x^{2} + 2 x - \\sin{\\left(x \\right)} + \\cos{\\left(x \\right)}\\right) e^{x} + 2}{\\left(e^{x} + 2 \\cos{\\left(x \\right)}\\right)^{2}}\\end{aligned}\n$$"} {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186488413 :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "2d5be94f-d42a-595a-a09d-2a3db0824964" :answer/type {:db/ident